# Copy to .env and adjust. Read by docker-compose.yml, and (optionally) sourced
# before running `scribe` natively so secrets stay out of the committed TOML.
#
# The containerised stack needs none of this to start: every value below has a
# working default, and the two real secrets — the blob signing secret and the
# phone's device token — are generated into the data volume on first start.
# Scribe reads SCRIBE_<SECTION>__<KEY> overrides at startup.

# --- what the phone connects to ---------------------------------------------
# The URL the mobile app and the worker use to reach the API. Leave it on
# loopback for a local trial; set it to this machine's Tailscale MagicDNS name
# to record from the phone (scripts/quickstart.ps1 -Tailscale does this for you).
# SCRIBE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://your-server.your-tailnet.ts.net

# --- ports (host side) -------------------------------------------------------
# Both are published on 127.0.0.1 only, never on the LAN.
SCRIBE_API_PORT=8443
# Postgres: 5433 rather than 5432, because a native Postgres often holds 5432.
POSTGRES_PORT=5433

# --- summaries and Q&A -------------------------------------------------------
# Needs the ollama profile:  docker compose --profile ollama up -d
# Pick a model your hardware can hold: gemma3:27b (24 GB VRAM), gemma3:12b
# (12 GB), llama3.2:8b (8 GB). Without an LLM the pipeline still produces
# transcripts, speaker labels, and search - only summaries and /ask are skipped.
SCRIBE_SUMMARIZE_MODEL=gemma3:12b

# --- logging -----------------------------------------------------------------
# info, debug, or a per-module filter such as scribe_pipeline=debug,info
SCRIBE_LOG=info

# --- native (non-container) runs ---------------------------------------------
# SCRIBE_DATABASE__URL=postgres://scribe:scribe@localhost:5433/scribe?sslmode=disable
# SCRIBE_STORAGE__SIGNING_SECRET=change-me-openssl-rand-hex-32
# SCRIBE_AUTH__REQUIRE_DEVICE_TOKEN=true

# --- self-update (only if you enable [update]) -------------------------------
# SCRIBE_UPDATE__TOKEN=change-me-openssl-rand-hex-32
# SCRIBE_UPDATE__PUBLIC_KEY=<64-hex from `scribe update keygen`>
